            <ArticleTitle>Win-win data sharing in neuroscience.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>112-116</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nmeth.4152</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most neuroscientists have yet to embrace a culture of data sharing. Using our decade-long experience at NeuroMorpho.Org as an example, we discuss how publicly available repositories may benefit data producers and end-users alike. We outline practical recipes for resource developers to maximize the research impact of data sharing platforms for both contributors and users.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
